-- One-time CloudTMS schema migration: banking_pay_stage2_work_reference_schema
-- Tables, columns, constraints and indexes for the Stage 2 candidate (tested extract A1 + A4 + A14).
-- [Worker AI amendment] Formerly CLEAN-START ONLY: the tested candidate had no backfill for existing Timesheet/payment rows (COMBINED_CANDIDATE G04,
-- STATUS H2 G-A4). The guard below therefore refuses to run on a database that already holds rows the new
-- work-reference / clock / protected-reference structures would need to describe. It never modifies data.
-- [Worker AU amendment REL-GENCOL] timesheets.bpay_work_key_v1 is an ORDINARY column maintained by the BEFORE
-- INSERT OR UPDATE trigger zz_bpay_timesheet_work_key_v1 (ENABLE ALWAYS, fires last) with exactly the former
-- generation expression, and guarded by CHECK bpay_timesheet_work_key_expression_v1 (NOT VALID here; validated by
-- the backfill). A STORED GENERATED column refused the product's whole-row Timesheet copies
-- (INSERT INTO public.timesheets SELECT (row).* in private._timesheet_route_version_legacy_v1 and
-- public.contract_week_manual_upsert_atomic: "cannot insert a non-DEFAULT value") and was NULL inside every BEFORE
-- trigger, which made timesheet_archive_row_guard_v1's to_jsonb(OLD)/to_jsonb(NEW) comparison refuse every Archive
-- transition (ARCHIVE_TRANSITION_METADATA_ONLY). Existing rows are still filled by the same table rewrite
-- (ADD COLUMN ... GENERATED ... STORED), then DROP EXPRESSION keeps those stored values: no trigger fires, no value
-- changes, and the lock is the one M1 already took.

\set ON_ERROR_STOP on

begin;

